# Cursor-specific instructions

[`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) is authoritative for shared agent policy,
including that Cursor Agent is the primary/default implementation agent.
Do not duplicate or override that file here.

Nested `AGENTS.md` files remain in force for their directories.

## Cursor Cloud

These notes apply when the agent is running in Cursor Cloud. They do not
require other agents to use Cursor, and they do not replace GitHub as the
source of truth.

- Toolchain: `bash`, `python3`, `jq`, `node`/`npm`, and `shellcheck` are all
  provided by the base environment. `shellcheck` is a system dependency (apt),
  not a repo package, so it is baked into the environment rather than the
  startup update script. The update script only runs `npm ci` for the single
  `markdownlint-cli2` dev dependency.
- `markdownlint-cli2` is available via npm in this environment. It is not a
  CI gate; follow `AGENTS.md` and scope it to files you actually touch.
- Portable tests listed in `AGENTS.md` run here without AI370 hardware and
  without network. On generic cloud VMs, treat Stage 1/Stage 2 `WARN` results
  as recorded facts per `AGENTS.md`, not as a broken environment.

## GitHub Projects MCP

Desktop Cursor loads [`.cursor/mcp.json`](../mcp.json). That file enables
the official GitHub Projects toolset (`projects_list`, `projects_get`,
`projects_write`) at `https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/x/projects`. Set
`GITHUB_MCP_PAT` in the local environment to a token with `project` scope
for writes (`read:project` is enough for reads). Do not put tokens in
`mcp.json` or `environment.json`.

Cloud Agents do not take that PAT from `mcp.json`. Add the same HTTP server
in the Cloud Agent MCP dropdown or Dashboard → Integrations & MCP, then
enable it for this environment:

- URL: `https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/x/projects`
- Header: `Authorization: Bearer <PAT with project scope>`

`mcpServerAllowlist` only permits a server; it does not install or
authenticate it. This Cloud Agent environment is dashboard-managed
(personal). Do not commit `.cursor/environment.json` only to add an
allowlist: a committed file would override the dashboard environment.

If this environment later becomes repository-managed, allow the Projects
server with:

```json
"mcpServerAllowlist": [
  {
    "name": "github-projects",
    "serverUrl": "https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/x/projects"
  }
]
```
